body:
## Research-session investigation brief

Owner request: turn the restrictions audit into an investigation for the original-game research session. **This issue is the dispatch entry point.** Establish original behavior and audit unsupported generalizations; implementation changes remain in the remake session. Start by reading the research repository instructions and current promoted findings, then follow its evidence/publication workflow.

### Purpose

Explain which restrictions are actual original rules, which were deliberate owner choices, and which arose from plausible assumptions in remake contracts or tests. The corrected negative-treasury funding rule is the motivating example: “never takes more than the source holds” was treated as original semantics despite an explicitly unresolved debt question. Do not use our task wording, helper reuse or passing tests as original evidence.

### Work packages, in order

1. **Signed supply and money arrows — highest priority.**
   - Paid foreign-city supply: reproduce the ordering of max(0, staged±step) versus min(stock, room, affordable tons). Use an army of10000 troops,206tons,purse100 beside a non-hostile city with330tons; inspect whether +100 stages -105 and Transfer returns105tons/refunds21talents. Include within-capacity decrement-to-zero, room0, over-cap room -1/-4/-5, empty-city and insufficient-purse controls. Test fleet targets separately if claiming their rule. Record exactly when records change and what Cancel/Close does. Recipient/source signs and division order matter.
   - Army-to-army money: A100/B1100, arrow nominally +100 into B; establish whether the signed step is -100, leaving A200/B1000. Test the opposite arrow, under/exactly-at/above-cap receiver, repeated presses and Cancel/OK. Verify Split's use of the same original handler before extending conclusions.
   - Existing build findings [1486](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1486) and [1487](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1487) have native remake probes; the original paid/army-money claims have different evidence strengths. Revalidate the exact code and run the missing controls rather than merely citing our reproduction.

2. **Per-unit partial army transfer and transport boundary.**
   - Reuse and verify existing original20-slot controls and U1/U3/U3b before running new experiments. Confirm source-slot iteration, destination slot assignment, which failing units remain, whether processing continues, and whether one or multiple refusal boxes follow.
   - Include target19 plus selected2 (one fits), mixed troop sizes around100000, and single-unit increases to15000/15499/15500 on30ships. Test both transfer directions, cancellation and recipient move changes. Distinguish arrow-time working-copy effects from final OK.
   - Deliver an exact admission/ordering matrix for build [1488](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1488)/[1489](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1489); do not copy Join-armies aggregate gates into this different caller.

3. **Human embark and mercenary-hire capacity — [research83](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/issues/83).**
   - Execute that child's5000/5001/5499/5500-on10ships controls for each caller. A transfer result does not establish embark/hire semantics. Separate dialog-opening gates from per-offer acceptance and subsequent cleanup.

4. **Unchanged transfer OK — [research84](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/issues/84).**
   - Execute no-editOK versus Cancel, reversed selected army and both-over-cap controls. Establish whether confirming alone triggers supply rebalance. Do not presume an unstaged dialog is a no-op.

5. **Targeted assumption sweep in the same manual economy/force-management family.**
   - Inventory guards/clamps that forbid an operation, cap a value, discard an overflow, force a value nonnegative, or turn an unchanged action into no effect. Review the exact original caller plus the historical task/test/owner-decision chain.
   - Start with the extra ±1000 transfer-money command ceiling, partial fleet-money cap/excess destination (existing build1326), embarked-army disband (residual question in closed build802), and carrier-link cleanup on all-mercenary desertion. These are leads, not additional confirmed bugs.
   - Classify command-interface policy and native model invariants separately from original GUI rules. Identify a player-reachable discriminating case before requesting a new correction.
   - Stop this pass at manual supply/funding, army/fleet transfer, embark/hire/disband and associated cleanup. This is not a request to re-research every battle/AI/serializer rule or delay results until the entire game is proved.

### Required deliverables / completion

- A promoted research report with one row per investigated restriction: exact original caller/site, claimed rule, source versus runtime evidence, whether the guard actually exists, boundary/ordering, tested cases and limits, corresponding remake location, existing issue/owner decision, and proposed intake disposition.
- Explicitly separate **proved original behavior**, **code-derived but unplayed**, **contradictory/unresolved**, **intentional design divergence**, and **CLI/model-only policy**. Keep status on GitHub labels; this is an evidence matrix, not a status document.
- For each new discrepancy, a minimal original input/action/output control and a remake comparison that actually distinguishes the competing rules. Existing probe code below is a comparison aid, never original evidence.
- Preserve EXE identity, exact findings/source revisions, private artifact location and reproducibility. State Wine/patched observer/stock EXE/native Windows categories honestly. Static evidence and Wine runs do not count as new Windows acceptance.
- Return a concise implementation handoff with exact rules and remaining choices linked to1486–1489 and83–84. Add further narrowly scoped research issues only for gaps found by the sweep; deduplicate first. Do not patch the remake, change owner policies, close implementation bugs on research completion or alter release gates.
- Publish useful bounded results as they are established; an unavailable Windows control is an explicit limitation rather than a reason to hold all other findings.

### Preserve deliberate choices and private evidence

Owner-approved no-wrap purse saturation, Transfer ships safety refusals (#1340), name/final-unit restrictions (#565), Improved affordability, QoL automatic-funding reserve and T216's safe refusal are outside automatic fidelity corrections. Verify their decision records; the task does not revoke them.

Use synthetic/private copies and preserve originals. Keep original bytes, screenshots, full decompilations and private save hashes out of public GitHub. Coordinate any owner-machine test so it never interrupts a running game. No original launch or research experiment has been executed by the build session for this brief.

---

## Audit evidence and reproducible remake probes (retained)

Continuation of the owner-requested [GUI provenance audit #82](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/issues/82), broadened to refusals, affordability, caps, partial operations and normalization after the manual treasury-debt error.

Audited source: remake [4d70275aac4e155c0370a3ee23525cf34450a908](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/tree/4d70275aac4e155c0370a3ee23525cf34450a908), research [865755e04f107afc38cdb496669d882e2551aca6](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/tree/865755e04f107afc38cdb496669d882e2551aca6). Parent session inspected economy/transfer helpers, importer/validation, diplomacy transitions and GUI staging; owner-authorized GPT-6.1 Sol/high inspected army/fleet/recruitment restrictions. This is an exploratory audit, not a milestone verdict.

## Concrete implementation discrepancies

| Finding | Evidence and observed remake behavior | Route |
|---|---|---|
| Paid supply stage floors away signed giveback | Original code-derived sequence floors amount BEFORE min(room); negative room can yield negative amount/refund. Native model probe:10000troops,206tons,purse100,foreignstock330 => room-105, staged0/no command; direct engine admits-105 and ends101tons/purse121. | [build1486](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1486) |
| Army-to-army money stage floors away signed pullback | Original code-derived row4 min(step,1000-receiver,giver) has no floor. Native model: giver100/receiver1100, +100 arrow => no command; reported signed rule would give200/1000. Row4 itself was not played in original. | [build1487](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1487) |
| Entire selected army transfer is rejected | Existing original Wine controls move units that fit, retain others and show a box. Native dispatcher: target19 units plus selected2 => rejected units-too-large, target stays19. Residual from closed umbrella802, not a new source discovery. | [build1488](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1488) |
| Army-transfer fleet capacity uses exact multiplication | Existing original Wine U3/U3b accepts15499 and refuses15500 on30ships. Native single499-unit transfer into15000 rejects fleet-cannot-carry. | [build1489](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1489) |

These are not all equivalent evidence categories:1486/1487 compare a reproduced remake calculation against promoted original code readings;1488/1489 additionally have the existing original Wine boundary controls. No new original game or native Windows acceptance was run.

## Questions requiring bounded original controls

- [Research83](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/issues/83): human EMBARK and mercenary HIRE use the same suspicious multiplication, but transfer's runtime result does not prove their callers. Measure5000/5001/5499/5500 on10ships separately with other gates valid.
- [Research84](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/issues/84): unchanged Army transfer OK is suppressed as a no-op; source reads unconditional supply rebalancing. Compare no-editOK/Cancel/reversedselection on over-cap inputs.
- The carried-army disband refusal remains an explicitly unresolved subquestion in [build802](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/802). Do not silently equate that umbrella's closure with a measured answer.
- [build1326](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1326) already covers partial fleet-money cap and excess-to-treasury behavior. No duplicate research task created.

## Unsupported wording / command-interface policies to keep distinct

TransferMoneyCommandHandler.cs:20–24/65–74 infers an independent ±1000 per-command ceiling from the same “capped at1000 per army or fleet” sentence used for the receiver purse cap. The source demonstrates a receiver cap and10/100 arrow steps, not an independent native game command of arbitrary magnitude. This is currently a command-interface restriction; audit has NOT shown a user-reachable original GUI mismatch. It should be labelled as such instead of promoted into another source-proven gameplay rule.

AutomaticResupply.cs retains stale prose claiming manual treasury transfer is balance-limited because no report permits debt. T219 already corrected the implementation; this is obsolete provenance wording, not evidence the old restriction still executes.

QuarterlyEconomySystem.cs:35–49 clears a carrier back-reference after all embarked mercenaries desert because native validation requires consistent links; it explicitly says original cleanup was unmeasured. That is a model-invariant adaptation, not proof of original lifecycle equivalence. No new defect established by static inspection.

## Checked restrictions that should NOT be silently removed

- Faithful manual treasury funding into debt: T219/research77 measured and corrected; explicit purse donors retain separate balance limits.
- Faithful recruitment/fortification allow debt; Improved refusal is an approved preset choice.
- Automatic human QoL funding retains the owner-configured reserve; manual debt evidence does not abolish it.
- [build1340](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1340) CLOSED not planned records OWNER retention of carrying-army and over100 Transfer ships refusals. This initially looked like unsupported defensive logic, but is now deliberate divergence.
- Purse0..32767 saturation instead of original wrap: approved owner no-wrap policy (PR758/963, T193); not an accidental1000 cap.
- Rename printableASCII/23char restrictions and final-unit disband refusal: explicit owner decisions under565.
- T216 AI no-safe-receiver atomic refusal: explicit owner-approved interim policy; do not replace it while investigating human transport.
- City population upper cap is source-supported and documented as nonbinding for legal classical growth inputs; no counterexample found.
- Supply purchase/automatic quantities, signed over-cap room, distinct dialog+1 army capacity, and mercenary pay's “pay last affordable-positive unit then floor” have concrete operation-specific research. Do not impose a generic nonnegative-stock/solvency rule across those paths.
- Original-save import negative-move normalization and parser safety/structural validation were inspected as explicit boundary policies. This audit did not establish an additional unsupported clamp there.

## Verification and limits

Four public synthetic native probes plus a direct engine comparison compiled against production code linked by the existing test assembly. Successful build and direct DLL execution exited0. Build had NU1900 because package vulnerability metadata could not reach nuget.org; no compile errors. No full test suite was run: there is no product change. Earlier quiet dotnet-run invocations failed without useful diagnostics; the recorded success is the explicit build followed by direct DLL execution, not those attempts.

Final scalar output:
```text
paid-dialog room=-105 staged=0 cost=0 command=<none>
engine admitted=-105 armySupply=101 armyMoney=121
army-money-arrow giver=100 receiver=1100 command=<none>
19plus2units rejected=True code=armies.army-transfer-units-too-large targetUnits=19
30ships15499 rejected=True code=armies.army-transfer-fleet-cannot-carry
```

The reproduction source uses only public synthetic testbed data and is retained below. No original bytes, owner saves or private hashes were used or posted. Source checkout stayed clean; ignored local scratch is rendered/assumptions-audit. No game launch, UI occupation, implementation patch, milestone change or release change.

This first pass concentrates on manually reachable economy and force-management boundaries, plus related normalization/provenance. It is not an exhaustive proof of every command, AI branch, serializer or numerical overflow behavior. Further audit should trace each guard to the exact original caller, inspect historical owner decisions and test whether the assertion distinguishes the original rule rather than merely repeating a task requirement.

## Reproduce the native checks

Create an ignored net10.0 console project under rendered/assumptions-audit referencing ../../tests/IC2.Engine.Tests/IC2.Engine.Tests.csproj. From repository root build with dotnet build rendered/assumptions-audit/Audit.csproj --no-restore --no-dependencies --disable-build-servers -m:1 /nr:false --nologo -v minimal after normal project restore/build, then run dotnet rendered/assumptions-audit/bin/Debug/net10.0/Audit.dll.

```csharp
using IC2.Engine.Model;
using IC2.Engine.Serialization;
using IC2.Engine.Economy;
using IC2.Engine.Tests.Core;
using IC2.Slice.UI;
var rules = GameDataRepository.Load("data").Resolve("classical-mediterranean").Ruleset;
var state = CoreTestbed.InitialState();
var army = new ArmyState("audit-army", "north", 3, 2, 4, 70, 100, 206, null, null, ValueList.Of(new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",10000,6,"Audit")));
var city = new CityState("audit-foreign","Audit",2,2,"south","south",90,330,0,100,100,0,ValueList<UnitSlot>.Empty);
state = state with { Armies=ValueList.Of(army), Cities=ValueList.Of(city), Fleets=ValueList<FleetState>.Empty };
var model = SupplyDialogModel.ForArmy(state,army,rules);
model.SelectProvider(0);
model.AdjustStaged(100);
Console.WriteLine($"paid-dialog room={model.ArmyRoomTons} staged={model.StagedTons} cost={model.StagedCostTalents} command={model.TransferStaged() ?? "<none>"}");
var result=SupplyPurchase.BuyForArmy(army, city, state.NationById("north")!, state.NationById("south")!,100,rules);
Console.WriteLine($"engine admitted={result.AdmittedTons} armySupply={result.Army.SupplyTons} armyMoney={result.Army.Money}");
if(model.ArmyRoomTons != -105 || model.StagedTons != 0 || model.TransferStaged() is not null || result.AdmittedTons != -105 || result.Army.Money != 121) throw new Exception("Probe unexpected");
var partner=army with { Id="audit-partner", X=4, Money=1100, SupplyTons=20 };
var transfer=ArmyTransferModel.ForArmies(army,partner,rules);
transfer.AdjustMoney(100);
Console.WriteLine($"army-money-arrow giver=100 receiver=1100 command={transfer.ComposeOk() ?? "<none>"}");
if(transfer.ComposeOk() is not null) throw new Exception("Money probe unexpected");
var donor=army with { Units=ValueList.Of(new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",1000,6,"one"),new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",1000,6,"two"),new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",1000,6,"keep")) };
var receiver=partner with { Units=ValueList.From(Enumerable.Range(0,19).Select(i=>new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",1000,6,"r"+i))), Money=0 };
var transferState=state with { Armies=ValueList.Of(donor,receiver) };
var dispatch=IC2.Engine.Tests.Armies.ArmiesTestbed.DispatcherWithRuleset(rules);
var partial=dispatch.Dispatch(transferState,new IC2.Engine.Armies.Commands.ArmyTransferCommand("north",donor.Id,receiver.Id,ValueList.Of(0,1),0,0,ValueList<int>.Empty,0,0));
Console.WriteLine($"19plus2units rejected={partial.IsRejected} code={partial.Code} targetUnits={partial.State.ArmyById(receiver.Id)!.Units.Count}");
if(!partial.IsRejected || partial.State.ArmyById(receiver.Id)!.Units.Count!=19) throw new Exception("Partial probe unexpected");
var carrier=new FleetState("audit-carrier","north",4,2,4,30,100,0,100,null,null,receiver.Id,null);
receiver=receiver with { Units=ValueList.Of(new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",15000,6,"aboard")), AboardFleetId=carrier.Id, CoveredTileCode=null };
donor=donor with { Units=ValueList.Of(new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",499,6,"small"),new UnitSlot(0,"light_infantry",1000,6,"keep")) };
transferState=state with { Armies=ValueList.Of(donor,receiver), Fleets=ValueList.Of(carrier) };
var boundary=dispatch.Dispatch(transferState,new IC2.Engine.Armies.Commands.ArmyTransferCommand("north",donor.Id,receiver.Id,ValueList.Of(0),0,0,ValueList<int>.Empty,0,0));
Console.WriteLine($"30ships15499 rejected={boundary.IsRejected} code={boundary.Code}");
if(!boundary.IsRejected) throw new Exception("Capacity probe unexpected");
```
